0337-negroni-bt-vendor-answers: bluetoothd's Apple/Broadcom vendor commands on the QCA6490 + the 0336 review fixes.

Phone [V] 2026-10-27 03:17 (logs/phone-log-20261027-031731.txt, bluetoothd[303]; kernel h4 log): after 0336 the
init goes on; then "BD_VSC_OLYMPIC_ANTENNA_PREF_B timedout waiting for controller", "Notifying BT Firmware
Crashed", restart reason 3602, every ~16 s. Cause [V disassembly of 20H392 bluetoothd]: _BCM_ByteStreamEventParser
(0x100126134) calls the command callback only when >= 2 bytes follow the status ("Invalid data size 0" logged just
before the timeout); our vendor answers had none. Every vendor command was already answered locally (none went to
the chip).

negroni_bt_shim.c:
- every vendor (OGF 0x3f) answer: status + negronibt_vscdata bytes (default 8): byte 0 = the first parameter byte
  (sub-opcode echo; _BCM_SubOpcodeChecker 0x100126390 checks it for 0xfce9), then zeros.
- status 0 for 0xfd3c, 0xfce9 (LE_META), 0xfce2 (OLYMPIC multiplex: sub 0x0b, 0x15), 0xfd48, 0xfd47
  (opcodes [V], names [I] from the error order); other vendor opcodes keep the 0333 table status.
- 0x2007 LE_Read_Advertising_Physical_Channel_Tx_Power: chip status 0x0c -> 0, TX power 0 dBm.
- review F1: 0x0c6d goes to the chip with Simultaneous_LE_Host rewritten to 0x00 (the chip lists the command, mask
  octet 24 bit 6; it rejected the 0x01 parameter); a remaining chip error is rewritten to status 0.
- review N1: 0x0c5a/0x0c5b are answered locally only after the 0x1002 mask was seen (s.cmds_known).
negroni_bt_shim_tx takes a writable packet (negroni_bt.h, negroni_bt_h4.c tx_packet).
negroni_bt_h4.c review F2: Command Status list without 0x0408, 0x205d -> 0x205e, + 0x042a, 0x0810, 0x2044, 0x2064,
0x2068, 0x206b, 0x206d.
negronibt_shimfix=0 turns the 0336/0337 fixes off (no effect with negronibt_shim=0).

